// obligation bytes, projections and persistence, not a fabric address alone.
//
// O_GPU_STEP_EXECUTION bindings:
// MF_EXEC sections 2-4,10-12,19-22 and MF_GAME sections 8-11,17:
// immutable snapshot, evaluation, propagation, governance, simultaneous commit,
// one logical tick boundary, and BLOCKED distinct from HALTED.
// 116 L09/L14, 117 W01-W04 and 096 require source-owned law and support.
// A1-A10/B1-B3/D2 supplies the world step; C1-C5/D1 excludes old physics.
// CANON governs operator/JTP behavior. Python reference code is not runtime.
// Lowering fixpoint epochs are not automatically STEP_FABRIC ticks.
//
// O_COMMIT bindings:
// MF_EXEC sections 2,10-12,19-21 and MF_GAME sections 10-13:
// successor constructed simultaneously; effects read committed successor only.
// A6/A7/D2 requires receipt NOT-SAME persistence and one governed chain extension;
// B1-B3 binds genesis. 116 L09/L11, 117 W02-W03 and 096 preserve support and W.
// C1-C5/D1 excludes retired update laws. CANON and MAIN-BANK-018 supplies the
// concrete persistence contact; AVR re-witness remains O_next, not a GPU gate.
//
// O_VECTOR_CONFORMANCE bindings:
// MF_EXEC sections 20-25 and MF_GAME sections 15-22 supplies reference contracts
// and evidence separation. 116 L11/L14, 117 W01-W04 and 096 bounds identity,
// causal support and generated coverage. A1-A10/B1-B3/D2 and CANON governs
// V1/V2 content; C1-C5/D1 excludes retired expectations. CONFORM remains V1/V2
// only until Devon accepts additional IDs from PROPOSED_ACCEPTANCE below.
//
