// Those original document bytes are not recovered in this binding. Current root
// MF_STATIC/MF_STATIC_VECTORS bytes do not substitute for them. STATIC acceptance
// candidates cite imported evidence, not promotion of those current documents.
// No complete executable fixture is claimed from a receipt's input_digest alone.
// REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE means proposed required classification, not current
// authority. Devon must accept the qualified ID before it enters CONFORM.
// REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY carries the original bounded receipt, no GPU credit.
// An accepted ID retains its source contract; no toy content or changed expected
// value is imported by shorthand. This table does not supply new vector bytes.
// IDs not listed are not proposed additions. Existing V1/V2 remain unchanged.
//
// ID | Contract | One-first-tick applicability | Proposed class
// STATIC/P04 | role-typed binary join | selected-step agreement consumes two roles | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/N05 | EXACTLY_ONE overconnection | duplicate arrival must not produce a tick result | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/N06 | binary role shape | two arrivals in one role cannot replace the other | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/N08 | witness payload compatibility | typed tick frames cannot silently cast witnesses | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/N09 | route endpoint identity | first-tick routes must resolve to their declared cells | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/N10 | declared input role | first-tick routing cannot invent a role | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// STATIC/C01 | text/visual PLACE confluence | visual editing is outside the supplied first tick | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/S01 | common immutable snapshot | all active cells of this step read the same predecessor | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S02 | peer-result isolation | same-step intermediate results cannot leak into evaluation | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S03 | downstream visibility at t+1 | one step must not collapse a route boundary | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S04 | immutable program | executing the selected tick cannot edit its fabric | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S05 | deterministic evaluation | repeated same tick inputs must preserve cell results | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S08 | atomic successor visibility | no partial first-tick state may become observable | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S09 | one synchronous route boundary | first-tick realization must expose its actual step boundary | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/S10 | V3.2-bound runtime authority, no FabricEdit payload | records a distinct admission scope, not D2 selection | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/F02 | complete binary frame | selected overlap evaluation consumes both routed readings | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/F03 | missing binary role remains incomplete | missing tick input supplies no default reading | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/F04 | staggered arrival then completion | multi-step arrival trajectory exceeds this one tick | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/F09 | over-arrival refusal | this tick cannot evaluate an overconnected frame | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/F10 | type-mismatch refusal | this tick cannot evaluate an ill-typed frame | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/F11 | partial custody, no timeout/default | incomplete input must survive the inspected step | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/F12 | static DRC plus complete frame shape | first-tick evaluation requires the declared role shape | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/P01 | EMPTY to ADMITTED | actual ingress must establish custody before evaluation | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/P02 | evaluation/propagation to next COMPLETED snapshot | distinguishes computation from committed custody | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/P09 | atomic mixed-phase commit | all participating first-tick slots commit together | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/P10 | release with retained receipt | later slot-release lifecycle is not this world's first commit | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/Q04 | partial input without progress is BLOCKED | first-tick diagnostic must not claim completion | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/Q07 | pending custody prevents HALTED despite empty obligations | first-tick status must inspect more than O | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/Q08 | fixed point with unresolved custody is BLOCKED | GPU fixpoint alone cannot authorize commit | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/Q11 | HALTED fixed point under CLOSED_RUN | closed-run continuation is beyond one externally supplied tick | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/Q12 | canonical BlockedReason order | first-tick diagnostics cannot depend on enumeration order | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/H07 | commit-construction order erasure | one successor cannot depend on host construction order | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/H10 | two permitted schedules, same successor | one-step schedule variation must preserve results | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/H12 | per-tick schedule changes preserve trajectory | a multi-tick trajectory is outside this spec | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/N01 | no EMPTY to COMPLETED shortcut | ingress cannot bypass admission during the first tick | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/N03 | no ADMITTED to DISCHARGED shortcut | evaluation and durable disposition cannot be skipped | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// EXEC/E02 | staggered binary chain to HALTED | full multi-step custody chain is reference evidence | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// EXEC/E04 | cross-region V3.2 runtime authority | its fabric-edit authority is not D2's gate selection | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// GAME/B01 | exact committed fabric target | tick bindings must name the fabric actually executed | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/B02 | declared ingress targets | kappa/E0/selection enter only through bound input contacts | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/B03 | declared egress outputs | world effects must read bound outputs only | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/B06 | mismatched fabric identity refused | wrong-fabric input cannot authorize this first tick | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T01 | sample once at tick boundary | supplied first-tick input is fixed for the step | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T02 | exactly one STEP_FABRIC | no hidden settle loop may stand in for the logical tick | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T03 | no mid-tick resampling | selected lift and basis cannot change during execution | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T04 | egress from committed successor | uncommitted candidate output cannot become world effect | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T05 | game update after fabric commit | D2 visible state must not precede committed fabric output | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/T08 | explicit multi-tick latency | later propagation is outside the first-tick vector scope | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// GAME/D06 | clean-process trace replay | the original multi-tick toy trace is reference only | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
// GAME/N01 | pending proposal cannot affect active run | unselected/unpromoted alternatives cannot alter commit | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/N03 | BLOCKED creates no default action | unresolved first-tick work cannot invent a displacement | REQUIRED_GPU_CONFORMANCE
// GAME/U01 | game/fabric/runtime UI together | presentation is outside first-tick execution | REFERENCE_EVIDENCE_ONLY
//
// Expected completed execution terminal: O_exec = {} only after those witnesses.
// O_next = { O_AVR_REPAIR_BOARD_RECEIPT, O_LATER_TICKS_AND_REENTRY,
//            O_R1_R3_GATE_READING_SELECTION, O_INDEPENDENT_BUILDER_COMPARISON }.
// O_AVR_REPAIR_BOARD_RECEIPT: PENDING, host-witnessed repair retained; not a GPU tick gate.
// O_LATER_TICKS_AND_REENTRY: PENDING, outside this one-tick scope.
// O_R1_R3_GATE_READING_SELECTION: PENDING by record; no reading chosen here;
// D2 NO/THIS marker-field agreement remains the bounded input.
// O_INDEPENDENT_BUILDER_COMPARISON: PENDING; this authoring/checking pass is not independent.
// W8 results and spec SHA256 belong to the external run record, not a self-hash.

// VECTORS -- exact byte-observable first-tick readbacks, not GPU memory layouts.
// Common reading: D2's reference encoding is UTF-8 sorted-key compact JSON,
// separators comma/colon, no BOM, no terminal newline. Array order is retained.
// D2's embedded digest strings are lowercase; the binding hashes below are uppercase.
// This is reference observation encoding, not a new production CANONICAL_BYTES law.
// Output projection: {"receipt": receipt, "state": state_body_with_chain}.
// state_body_with_chain contains D2 state_body's field/entities and the actual chain.
// field is the complete 480-entry sorted flag/reading list, never a sparse substitute.
// receipt_reading is THIS when discharged or opened has content; NO when both have none.
// These are pre-numeric carrier readings, not truth values; the complete receipt remains.
// Genealogy RECEIPT_READING_001: Devon's instruction replaces D2 tick.py:100-103
// receipt_empty with receipt_reading. D2 is reproduced except this field and its
// downstream tick-link/output digests. No other state or receipt content changes.
// The input carries kappa, E0, complete genesis initial_state, entity, kind, target,
// and exact selected_lift. initial_state must be the genesis produced from kappa/E0.
// The supplied lift is a choice input, not a host ordering rule or a fabricated token.
// The runtime stages establish its membership, basis and authorization before commit.
// Derivation contact: D2:47-53,61-108. Expected bytes are frozen before any candidate.
// No expected-output file may supply the candidate's world state.
//
// Exact local names for the hand derivation (each tuple is [site,edge,triad]):
// t  = ["C:N|U0","C:N|U1","D:N"]
// t4 = ["C:N|U0","C:N|U4","D:N"]
// t2 = ["C:N|U1","C:N|U2","D:N"]
// ea = ["C:N|U0","D:N"]; eb = ["C:N|U1","D:N"];
// ec = ["C:N|U0","C:N|U1"].
// f=["D:N",ea,t]; g=["C:N|U0",ea,t]; h=["D:N",eb,t]; j=["D:N",ea,t4].
// gGamma=["C:N|U0",ec,t]; gTau=["C:N|U0",ea,t4].
// hDelta=["C:N|U1",eb,t]; hTau=["D:N",eb,t2].
// Initial kappa=f, E0={"e1":f}; f reads THIS, the other 479 flags read NO.
// Each pair and the pair list use D2's lexicographic incidence ordering.
// V1: delta(f)=g. Discharged {(f,h),(f,j)}; opened {(g,gGamma),(g,gTau)}.
// The pair (f,g) remains a wall: THIS/NO becomes NO/THIS.
// V2: gamma(f)=h. Discharged {(f,g),(f,j)}; opened {(h,hDelta),(h,hTau)}.
// The pair (f,h) remains a wall. All other unchanged overlaps retain their reading.
// For either vector the selected lift has from=f, via=f, to=g or h, and reading
// {"discharged":2,"opened":2,"walls_after":3}. The two receipts are distinct.
// Genesis record follows D2:52-53; tick record follows D2:100-103 except
// RECEIPT_READING_001 above, with ONE new link.
// Mechanical expansion/hashing of this hand-derived data is retained in
// author_vectors.mjs; it is authoring support, not a runtime or independent builder.

// V1 FIRST_TICK(V1.input.json)
//    argument_1 V1.input.json sha256 28093717ACC694FACC3B635701A22AFF37DDB09FB0447774BACC700647F262BE
//    input_bytes 32842; kind site; target "C:N|U0"; selected_lift f -> g via f.
//    expected_sha256 69786966E9B5D66A2078D29C43E1F1511545786AB07BF562E37D91205085B588
//    expected_bytes_count 33563; expected_file V1.expected.json.
//    origin D2 definitions plus hand-derived adjacent-site receipt; no candidate output.
//    execution NOT_RUN.

// V2 FIRST_TICK(V2.input.json)
//    argument_1 V2.input.json sha256 DC46E239B9D693AF25DC3D7005718060230D31AC9CA057F7ECCCF73968AA2C8E
//    input_bytes 32847; kind edge; target eb; selected_lift f -> h via f.
//    expected_sha256 BD0492B4CAC427432CC3251EB27FC997C0D5EFF2862ECBC10A89B9AC19F1AD0F
//    expected_bytes_count 33548; expected_file V2.expected.json.
//    origin D2 definitions plus hand-derived adjacent-edge receipt; no candidate output.
//    execution NOT_RUN.

// Witness correspondence, content of HOW(GOES_WITH), not an additional law:
// JTP order WHAT,WHERE,WHICH,WHEN,FOR_WHAT,HOW,WHENCE maps by name to EMIT
// WHAT,HOW,FOR_WHAT,WHERE,WHICH,WHEN,WHENCE via [0,3,4,5,2,1,6].
// motif = 7*family+witness in the named JTP order; EMIT cell = 7*op+witness
// in its own named order. No raw-index equality or 480-flag/105-cell equality.
// The pure-gate section 9.2 object is NOT the legacy MALCFU24 ObligationV1 core.
// Its layout is supplied; D2-specific source-to-payload realization remains O_exec.
// Existing EMIT CONFORM IF_THEN is retained only for its V1/V2 canonical profile.
// Genealogy: historical 8E69D9C5 checker prefix discrepancy stays OPEN_NOT_SAME,
// not a W8 gate. No inherited form or hardware discharge is reopened here.
